n, Amar,econtributor.1 aHusain, Amin,eeditor.1 aKapadia, Jesal,econtributor.1 aKhanna, Shyam,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n938029381 aLarson, Ann,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n820126761 aLorde, Audre,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n500422981 aMacPhee, Josh,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20030159451 aMaharawal, Manissa McCleave,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20220732461 aMcKee, Yates,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20110098581 aMerz, John,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20081124271 aMillar, Andi,econtributor.1 aMirzoeff, Nicholas,econtributor.1 aMohit, Nastaran,econtributor.1 aMouffe, Chantal,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n791434991 aMuriente, Sofía Gallisá,econtributor.1 aNastasia, Isabelle,econtributor.1 aPerisic, Aleksandra,econtributor.1 aReed, Conor Tomás,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20210185181 aRibellarsi, Eric,econtributor.1 aRoss, Andrew,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n853066651 aRuggiero, Greg,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n921215681 aSchneider, Nathan,econtributor.1 aShami, Muna,econtributor.1 aVarela, Alejandro,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20091830282 aAnonymous Labor Organizer,eContributor.2 aArabic Translators,eContributor.2 aLibrary Stack,edistributor.2 aNitasha S,eEditor.2 aOccupy Wall Street,eContributor.2 aStrike Debt Space Team,eContributor.2 aStrike Debt,eContributor.2 aTidal Family,eContributor.40zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://www.librarystack.org/block-by-block/yLibrary StackxProvider: Library StackxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxls4zTo create lists or check out books that are not open access, users must create a Library Stack account.xls1375742uhttps://www.librarystack.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/12/Tidal_4-1-480x630.jpgzCover Image Preview  aeLoaderRecord xls4ffi0355fd64-ff66-4267-bb5a-1bd4e5ea122bs88221969-6527-45a7-8f56-a8fd24c1dbf207322cam a2200745 i in0000024225020250403134809.0241001t20242024caua     bc   000 0 eng d  a9781636811376qhardcover  a163681137Xqhardcover 9agls21066143  aMYAbengerdacMYAdOCLCOdPULdCRUdJQFdYDXdTEUdYDXdUtOrBLW 4aNX650.E58bB74 202404a700.10322300aBreath(e) :btoward climate and social justice /corganized by Glenn Kaino and Mika Yoshitake13aBreath :btoward climate and social justice 1aLos Angeles, CA :bArmand Hammer Museum of Art and Cultural Center, Inc. ;aNew York, NY :bDelmonico Books · D.A.P.,c2024 2aNew York, NY :bDelmonico Books available through ARTBOOK/D.A.P. 4c[2024] 4c©2024  a256 pages :bcolor illustrations ;c26 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  astill imagebsti2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aPublished on the occasion of the exhibition Breath(e): Toward Climate and Social Justice, organized and presented by the Hammer Museum, Los Angeles as part of PST ART: Art & Science Collide. The exhibition is guest curated by Glenn Kaino and Mika Yoshitake with Jennifer Buonocore-Nedrelow, PST Fellow, September 15, 2024--January 5, 2025  aFeatured artists include: Brandon Ballengée, Mel Chin, Tiffany Chung, Ron Finley, LaToya Ruby Frazier, Cannupa Hanska Luger, Ryoji Ikeda, ikkibawiKrrr, Michael Joo, Danil Krivoruchko, Xin Liu, Yoshitomo Nara, Otobong Nkanga, Roxy Paine, Garnett Puett, Rob Reynolds, Sandy Rodriguez, Sarah Rosalena, Bently Spang, Mika Tajima, Clarissa Tossin, Lan Tuazon, Yangkura, Jin-me Yoon, and Zheng Mahler  aIncludes bibliographical references0 aDirector's Foreword / Ann Philbin -- Curatorial Acknowledgments / Glenn Kaino and Mika Yoshitake -- Breath(e): Point of No Return / Mika Yoshitake -- A Breath Within a Breeze / Glenn Kaino -- VOICE. Why I Do What I Do and Why You Shoul Do What I Do Too! / Ron Finley -- Object Descriptions / Jennifer Buonocore-Nedrelow -- LIFE CYCLES. Futures of Breathfulness / T. J. Demos -- King Philip Chewed Old Fish Gut Soup / Lan Tuazon -- LIVING KNOWLEDGE. Until All of Us Can Breathe / Leah Penniman -- Apisculptures / Garnett Puett -- BALANCE. Indigenous Cultural Continuity = Survival of the Human Species / Sherri Mitchell, Weh'na Ha'mu Kwasset -- Through the World Line / Cannupa Hanska Luger -- RADICAL PRESENCE. Alchemy for Our Times / Kimbery Bain -- Potential Energy / Mika Tajima -- VISIBILITY. A Letter to the Sky: On Breath(e) / Chus Martínez -- IOV / Mel Chin -- The Book We Didn't Make & The One That We Did / Brian Johnson and Silas Munro -- Artist and Contributor Biographies -- Exhibition Checklist  aThe exhibition considers environmental art practices that address the climate crisis and anthropogenic disasters and their inescapable intersection with issues of equity and social justice. Breath(e) features works by more than 20 artists, including works by Mel Chin, Ron Finley, Cannupa Hanska Luger, Garnett Puett, and Lan Tuazon, commissioned specially for this exhibition. Breath(e) was conceived during the height of the global COVID-19 pandemic and America's racial reckoning in 2020, and as such explores pressing issues related to the ethics of climate justice, while proposing pragmatic and philosophical approaches to spur discussion and resolution. The exhibition strives to challenge and deconstruct polarized political attitudes surrounding climate justice in America and offers new perspectives around land and indigenous rights of nature 0aEnvironmentalism in artvExhibitions. 0aEnvironmental protection in artvExhibitions. 0aEnvironmental degradation in artvExhibitions. 0aSocial justice in artvExhibitions. 0aInstallations (Art)vExhibitions.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008104691 0aClimate justicevExhibitions. 0aEnvironmental justicevExhibitions. 6aJustice climatique0(CaQQLa)000