O mon Fernand.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8783223612aTchaikovsky, Peter Ilich,d1840-1893.tOrleanskai︠a︡ deva.pArii︠a︡ Ioanny.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9605173012aMeyerbeer, Giacomo,d1791-1864.tProphète.pAh! mon fils.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n9708294512aVerdi, Giuseppe,d1813-1901.tAïda.pOhimè! morir mi sento.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n9706608212aWagner, Richard,d1813-1883.tRing des Nibelungen.pWalküre.pSo ist es denn aus mit den ewigen Göttern.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no2001053419  aRobert Baxter collection 0aBiographies in music.  aSUL/MUSIC/catalogedby/Flourish-CAM/202411  aSUL/MUSIC/gift/kevkishi/20241205/Baxter  b36105234619786cMCD 74540n1lMusic PAGE-MU (MUS-PAGE-MU)  aC0bSTFffs32244036-ee73-411e-9631-55de5e6e1506i046180b1-7558-49db-80d4-f63d6ae0e4a606647nab a2200985ui in0000030275920250403134818.0m||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu221230s2013||||xx || | |||||||   ||eng|d  als115702  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00aMapping Asia 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bAsia Art Archive,c2013  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier0 aField Notes (Asia Art Archive) ;v3  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"The third issue of Field Notes addresses the constant question of how AAA defines "Asia" but is in no way intended to survey or comprehensively cover any of the entry points in how to map Asia. Instead, it is to point to the entanglements between them and provide an additional space, along with AAA's other projects, to construct reference points and connections across time, sites, and geographies. We realize that there is something about the positioning of Asia, Art, and Archive next to each other that presupposes a mapping process. Acknowledging both the value and limitations of the map as a tool, AAA has attempted to trace the phenomena, practices, discourses, and developments in contemporary art in Asia by building up a collection based on breadth (via a widespread network of researchers, advisors, collaborators, and friends) and depth (through focused thematic archival projects). As such, we are practicing a mapping of Asia that no longer depends on the map as artifact, but as something that lives and continues to unfold. And while we believe that AAA's collection allows for a comparison of cross-regional histories and ideological networks, we must stress the importance of reading its material in conjunction with other mapping and archival initiatives..."--cprovided by distributor  aStandard Copyright10aArchives.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500691310aArt criticism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500798910aArt, Modern--21st century.10aCartography.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8502051510aGeopolitics.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8505419210aGlobalization.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh9901017910aHistoriography.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8506121110aImperialism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8506462810aPostcolonialism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh9700783510aTerritory, National.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8513411017aArchives.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008140300http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81403017aArt criticism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008154920http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81549217aCartography.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008480250http://id.worldcat.org/fast/84802517aColonies.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009681260http://id.worldcat.org/fast/86845617aContemporary Art.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0115982017aGeopolitics.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009410450http://id.worldcat.org/fast/94104517aGlobalization.2fast0(OCoLC)fst017362290http://id.worldcat.org/fast/94353217aHistoriography.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009582210http://id.worldcat.org/fast/95822117aTerritory, National.2fast0(OCoLC)