2lacc04aThe encyclopaedia of Islam three /cedited by Marc Gaborieau [and others] ; with Roger Allen [and others]10aEncyclopedia of Islam14aEI three3 aEncyclopaedia of Islam 33 aEncyclopedia of Islam 33 aEI 33 aEI313aEncyclopedia of Islam three  a3rd ed 1aLeiden [Netherlands] ;aBoston :bBrill,c2007-<2023> 4c2007-<2023>  avolumes :billustrations (some color) ;c27 cm  amultiple unit2rdami  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  gmonochrome2rdapcc  gpolychrome2rdacc  pillustration2rdaill  abibliographybbibliography  a"EI three"--Cover  a"1873-9830"--Title page verso  aEditors vary: 2 edited by Gudrun Krämer ... [et al.]; 3 (2013) edited by Kate Fleet, Gudrun Krämer; Denis Matringe, John Nawas, and Everett Rowson; 4 (2014) edited by Kate Fleet, Gudrun Krämer; Denis Matringe, John Nawas, and Everett Rowson; 1-3 (2015) edited by Kate Fleet, Gudrun Krämer; Denis Matringe, John Nawas, and Everett Rowson; 1-<3> (2016) edited by Kate Fleet, Gudrun Krämer; Denis Matringe, John Nawas, and Everett Rowson; <2017-> edited by Kate Fleet, Gudrun Krämer; Denis Matringe, John Nawas, and Everett Rowson  a"Four substantial segments each year, both online and in print."--Publisher's website  aAlso available online  aIncludes bibliographical references  a"Brill's Third Edition of the Encyclopaedia of Islam (EI3) is an entirely new work with new articles reflecting the great diversity of current scholarship. The EI3 appears in four substantial parts each year, both online and in print. The new scope includes comprehensive coverage of Islam in the twentieth century, attention to Muslim minorities all over the world, full attention to social science as well as humanistic perspectives."--cPublisher0 aVol. 2007-1. Abbas Hilmi II -- India (Hind)0 aVol. 2007-2. Aaron -- Ayyubids0 aVol. 2007-3. Aban b. Uthman b. Affan -- al-Bayati, Abd al-Wahhab0 aVol. 2008-1. Aaron ben Elijah of Ni