strategy, Venus and Venice, the sunset as a propitious direction, the drawing of shadows, camouflage, Vesper Lynd and the Vesper cocktail (both inventions from the pen of Ian Fleming) are the constellation points that propagate from the term vesper and that "Vesper" 8 plans to illuminate."--cprovided by distributor  aCC BY-NC-ND10aArchitects.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500656510aArchitectural criticism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500658310aArchitecture.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500661110aCity planning.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8502628210aHistoriography.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8506121110aPhotographic criticism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8600395510aSpace (Architecture)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8512590717aArchitects.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008131140http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81311417aArchitectural criticism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008131790http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81317917aArchitectural Space.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0112760117aArchitecture.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008133460http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81334617aHistoriography.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009582210http://id.worldcat.org/fast/95822117aPhotographic criticism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst010616370http://id.worldcat.org/fast/106163717aUrbanism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00862177 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026139 7aPeriodicals.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014116410http://id.worldcat.org/fast/14116411 aAquilar, Giorgia,eeditor.1 aArrighi, Laura,eeditor.1 aAzzariti, Giorgio,econtributor.1 aBelloni, Francesca,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20171481261 aBergamo, Francesco,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20170293781 aBersani, Giulia,eeditor.1 aBoano, Camillo,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20050958271 aBoffi, Guido,econtributor.1 aBorgherini, Malvina,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authoritie